    "created_at": "2020-08-18T21:58:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-18T21:58:00Z",
    "body": ">code shouldn’t be relying on the PSL or eTLD+1\r\n\r\nIn world where we're using SiteForCookies for numerous things (like SameSite cookies) and things as obscure as whether credential prompts may show for cross-site-images (https://textslashplain.com/2020/08/17/seamless-single-sign-on/) it would be super useful to be able to reliably understand the browser's understanding of what constitutes the registrable domain portion of an origin.\r\n\r\nFor instance, today, given https://deeply.nested.fuzzle.bunnies.io/, how would you as a browser expert go about determining what the current Chrome Beta build thinks is the registrable domain? Even using the Devtools, I have no idea how to do it short of creating convoluted test cases that probe for whether cookies can be created and whatnot.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
