    "created_at": "2023-03-31T16:15:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-31T16:15:13Z",
    "body": "At Discord we are interested in following best practices when displaying URLs to users to ensure they can understand the implications of a navigation and decide with confidence. eTLD+1 falls into these best practices, but it is not practical to ship the entire public suffix list in our web app.\r\n\r\nAlso I'm not entirely sure that an API on `URL` is exactly what we would want in this case. A separate API specifically designed for displaying URLs may be more suitable (maybe something like a URL segmenter?). Either way, eTLD+1 functionality would be great to have.",
